Subject: Adapt schema fetches overflow files and attribution for sandbox

Why: In kube-agents' sandbox, (1) `gcloud` goes through the credential proxy (which forwards no shell env vars) and direct REST egress is blocked, so upstream's mandatory `references/attribution.md` block and file waste a turn on no-op env vars and unreachable `curl` commands (removing both prevents agents from opening the orphaned file); (2) the sandbox has a deny-all-internet NetworkPolicy, so schema fetches to GitHub and `kueue.sigs.k8s.io` stall 8-16s in all modes (including `live` `KueueConfiguration` fetches and `validate_report.py`) unless `--no-remote-schema` is passed on every command (a separate `export` does not persist across Hermes SSH tool calls); and (3) gateway truncated-output overflow paths live on the gateway pod and return `FileNotFoundError` inside the sandbox (`agents/platform/AGENTS.md`), whereas `full_report_file` beside `--ledger-path` is local to the sandbox.
Local-Issue: none (adoption of gke-kueue-troubleshooting from google/skills)
Eval-Case: kueue-troubleshooting-mixed-flavor-tas-probe
Upstream-Issue: none (specific to this repository)
Retire-When: never; sandbox NetworkPolicy, credential-proxy attribution, and gateway overflow isolation are this repository's

